{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "08WE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Hom$", "MATH_0002": "\\begin{equation}\n\\label{equation-adjunction}\nC(\\bullet_1 \\otimes_R \\bullet_2) \\cong \\Hom_R(\\bullet_1, C(\\bullet_2)): \n\\text{Mod}_R \\times \\text{Mod}_R \\to \\text{Mod}_R\n\\end{equation}", "MATH_0003": "$f: M_1 \\otimes_R M_2 \\to \\mathbf{Q}/\\mathbf{Z}$", "MATH_0004": "$m_1 \\mapsto \n(m_2 \\mapsto f(m_1 \\otimes m_2))$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\xymatrix@C=9pc{\nC(M) \\ar@<1ex>[r] \\ar@<-1ex>[r] & C(N) \\ar[r] & C(P)\n}\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$\\text{Mod}_R$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n\\xymatrix@C=9pc{\nC(M \\otimes_R Q) \\ar@<1ex>[r] \\ar@<-1ex>[r] & C(N \\otimes_R Q) \\ar[r] & C(P \n\\otimes_R Q)\n}\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$Q \\in \\text{Mod}_R$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-hom-from-tensor-product-variant}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-adjunction}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c90102151abbca6adde9839b01ea954fa0cc0ccf6397a065b38a42bd73a4dec1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ec60dbede91929c864a943c9c621334075e83732c847214f7a47f47ecc6ee4c6", "source_text": "We will use frequently the standard adjunction between <MATH_0001> and tensor \nproduct, in the form of the natural isomorphism of contravariant functors\n<MATH_0002>\ntaking <MATH_0003> to the map <MATH_0004>. See\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nA corollary of this observation is that if\n<MATH_0005>\nis a split coequalizer diagram in <MATH_0006>, then so is\n<MATH_0007>\nfor any <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8adb3f689f5a17c64dc2d86487f33ac1a0aae7dd13c80ae1791d667ece84e9a2", "unit_id": "tag:08WS:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "08WE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$R$", "MATH_0002": "$f: M \\to N$", "MATH_0003": "$\\text{Mod}_R$", "MATH_0004": "$C(f): C(N) \\to C(M)$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-split-surjection}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:89e626d66b180018b1ad2d29744f23b6348a73405d8630a588dac39a2a86a2c5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d3d97db44481de3aacd4b70ecafcd8e5781a7f65dff4322e9436641b4981c44c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a ring. A morphism <MATH_0002> in <MATH_0003> is universally\ninjective if and only if <MATH_0004> is a split surjection.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:eaa21f55e9d1ba6fc0cef2a228efb8d1dc3addd6b75eef77847414c754790368", "unit_id": "tag:08WU:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "08WE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$P \\in \\text{Mod}_R$", "MATH_0002": "$$\n\\xymatrix@C=9pc{\n\\Hom_R( P, C(N)) \\ar[r]_{\\Hom_R(P,C(f))} \\ar[d]^{\\cong} &\n\\Hom_R(P,C(M)) \\ar[d]^{\\cong} \\\\\nC(P \\otimes_R N ) \\ar[r]^{C(1_{P} \\otimes f)} & C(P \\otimes_R M ).\n}\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$1_{C(M)} \\otimes f: C(M) \\otimes_R M \\to \nC(M) \\otimes_R N$", "MATH_0005": "$P = C(M)$", "MATH_0006": "$1_{C(M)} \\in \\Hom_R(C(M), C(M))$", "MATH_0007": "$g \\in \\Hom_R(C(N), C(M))$", "MATH_0008": "$C(f)$", "MATH_0009": "$C(f)$", "MATH_0010": "$1_{P} \\otimes f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-adjunction}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-C-is-faithful}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c5860af56fadc0d96ac13811047cf35bca615600f98fdc35c5de979a2b086ed4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:eca1b452c6bfe80bbf851e252c7da6a5eb9729b0e289bbd800143c811fd26ee3", "source_text": "By (<REF_0001>), for any <MATH_0001> we have a \ncommutative diagram\n<MATH_0002>\nIf <MATH_0003> is universally injective, then <MATH_0004> is injective,\nso both rows in the above diagram are surjective for <MATH_0005>. We may thus \nlift\n<MATH_0006> to some <MATH_0007> splitting \n<MATH_0008>.\nConversely, if <MATH_0009> is a split surjection, then \nboth rows in the above diagram are surjective,\nso by Lemma <REF_0002>, <MATH_0010> is injective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:51f4b784fe506a7aac11c26dbecb106ef139c60e6eec5ebf1ac71df0dbe94f3e", "unit_id": "tag:08WU:proof"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "08WE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f: M \\to N$", "MATH_0002": "$\\text{Mod}_R$", "MATH_0003": "$g$", "MATH_0004": "$C(f)$", "MATH_0005": "$C(1_P \\otimes f)$", "MATH_0006": "$P \\in \\text{Mod}_R$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Hom_R(P, \nC(f))$", "MATH_0008": "$P$", "MATH_0009": "$g \\circ \\bullet$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-adjunction}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-functorial-splitting}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:56ce29d7292dfdac4288b2d831e3f4bb51890720f4cd5e91835ac2a3a8b5d978", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6df32e3ebb697676f9e21b8476a3b553816f7cf61e2addf8ec22aece4f927502", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a universally injective morphism in <MATH_0002>. By \nchoosing a splitting\n<MATH_0003> of <MATH_0004>, we may construct a functorial splitting of <MATH_0005> \nfor each <MATH_0006>.\nNamely, by (<REF_0001>) this amounts to splitting <MATH_0007>  functorially in <MATH_0008>,\nand this is achieved by the map <MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:727eab0f1290f731d4b57628044aac7d17f37ea3d3a138bed60a7ebd9c12aedf", "unit_id": "tag:08WV:statement"}
